<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Raciąż</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1404</span> · Also known as Peace of Raciąż</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Raciąż was signed in May 1404 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. It confirmed the Order's possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a>, which linked its lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, and allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> to buy back <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dobrzyn-land">Dobrzyń Land</a>, which had been pledged to the Order. The settlement collapsed when Samogitia revolted in 1409.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-raciaz.jpg" alt="Treaty of Raciąż" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PL_1_1_122_0001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
